$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-videos
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta name="twitter:site" content="@MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://maizegdb.org/community/videos">
<meta property="og:title" content="Community videos | MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:description" content="Recorded talks on the history of maize genetics and the Maize Genetics Meeting, and six short demonstrations of controlled pollination of maize.">

<a class="mgdb-skip-link" href="#videos-main">Skip to main content</a>

<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-videos-page" id="videos-main">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/maize_history">Community</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Videos</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="videos-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg class="videos-hero-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" role="img" aria-label="Film strip with a play symbol">
        <rect x="9" y="21" width="78" height="54" rx="6" fill="#235c37" />
        <rect x="9" y="33" width="78" height="30" fill="#e8f4ec" />
        <g fill="#e8f4ec">
          <rect x="14" y="24" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="29" y="24" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="44" y="24" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="59" y="24" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="74" y="24" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" />
          <rect x="14" y="66" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="29" y="66" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="44" y="66" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="59" y="66" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="74" y="66" width="8" height="6" rx="1.5" />
        </g>
        <path d="M41 39 L60 48 L41 57 Z" fill="#d99a0b" />
      </svg>
      <strong>Community<br />Videos</strong>
      <span>Talks and demonstrations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="videos-title">Recorded talks and field demonstrations.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">The history of maize genetics and of the Maize Genetics Meeting in $(talk_count) recorded talks, and $(pollination_count) short demonstrations of controlled pollination &#8212; $(total_runtime_spoken) in all. Every one plays on this page, and nothing is loaded from Vimeo until you press play.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#videos-talks" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Talks</a>
    <a href="#videos-pollination">Controlled pollination</a>
    <a href="#videos-nobel">Nobel lecture</a>
    <a href="#videos-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="videos-talks" aria-labelledby="videos-talks-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="videos-talks-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Talks</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="videos-grid videos-grid-wide">$(talk_cards)</div>
  </section>

  <section id="videos-pollination" aria-labelledby="videos-pollination-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="videos-pollination-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Controlled pollination</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="videos-lead">Clips filmed at the University of Missouri-Columbia, in the order the procedure runs. The step numbers are the numbered sections of <a href="/controlled_pollination">Controlled Pollination of Maize</a>, the written protocol they illustrate &#8212; two clips carry 4.2 because that step covers both bagging the tassel and the pollination itself.</p>

    <div class="videos-grid videos-grid-narrow">$(pollination_cards)</div>
  </section>

  <section id="videos-nobel" aria-labelledby="videos-nobel-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="videos-nobel-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Nobel lecture</h2></div>
    </div>

    <article class="videos-nobel-card">
      <div class="videos-nobel-body">
        <p class="videos-nobel-meta">Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine &#183; 8 December 1983</p>
        <h3>Barbara McClintock, &#8220;The Significance of Responses of the Genome to Challenge&#8221;</h3>
        <p>McClintock was awarded the 1983 prize for her discovery of transposable elements in maize. She delivered this lecture in Stockholm on 8 December 1983.</p>
        <p class="videos-nobel-note"><strong>The recording is no longer online.</strong> This page used to embed the Nobel Foundation's video file; that host stopped resolving, and nobelprize.org no longer offers the recording on its own lecture page. The text of the lecture is still published there.</p>
        <p class="videos-nobel-links">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/1983/mcclintock/lecture/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the lecture</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="https://www.nobelprize.org/uploads/2018/06/mcclintock-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="videos-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="videos-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="videos-related-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Related resources</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/controlled_pollination">
          <strong>Controlled Pollination of Maize</strong>
          <span>The written protocol these clips illustrate, step by step, with precautions and supplies</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/maize_history">
          <strong>Maize genetics community history</strong>
          <span>A century of maize genetics, the cooperators, and the meetings these talks describe</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/maize_meeting">
          <strong>Maize Genetics Meeting</strong>
          <span>The annual meeting, its past programs, and the archived meeting websites</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/podcast">
          <strong>NCGA podcasts</strong>
          <span>National Corn Growers Association podcasts recorded with maize researchers, 2012-2013</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://vimeo.com/user3840197" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>MaizeGDB on Vimeo</strong>
          <span>The MaizeGDB video account, where eight of the nine videos on this page are published</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
)
